  Notes on Celery Entrypoint
    For whatever reason, the "broker" parameter that's fed into the main Celery
      constructor needs to be "broker_url" in a settings file, so with the namespace
      applied to the Django settings, it became "CELERY_BROKER_URL".
    Once that setting was correct, I simply ran an "sh" instance in the Django container
      using docker exec and used that session to get the right command for the
      celery binary. Once the config and entrypoint was correct, I was able to
      run a celery task inside the Django CLI that was defined in pokemon.tasks
      and could run an ORM operation, saving a Pokemon model
